      ],
      "description": "PRIMARY LOAD INDICATOR FOR llm2. Since MIG blocks DCGM_FI_DEV_GPU_UTIL, power draw is the most direct available signal of real GPU work: an idle card sits near its floor, a busy one climbs toward its cap. Note this is per PHYSICAL GPU, so on llm2 it reflects both MIG partitions combined, not each slice separately.",
      "title": "Power Draw — primary load indicator for llm2",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
